{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "Plural forms of the kit's count copy. Strings carry the CLDR `one` and `other` forms (Vue: a message value {one?, other, …}; native: a <field>One sibling field of the `other` field, pluralOf in strings/en.json). The kit picks `one` when the locale's CLDR cardinal category for the non-negative integer count is one, else `other` (few, many, two and zero fall back to other in the natives; a Vue tree may carry them). Vue reads the category from Intl.PluralRules and its test checks that table against it; the natives implement the table below as a pure function.",
  "rules": {
    "families": {
      "none": "never one",
      "is1": "one when n = 1",
      "is0or1": "one when n is 0 or 1",
      "mod10is1": "one when n % 10 = 1 and n % 100 ≠ 11"
    },
    "languages": {
